# arena_extend_strategy=kSameAsRequested in the ONNX template, 2026-11-26.
#
# Why: section 5 of references/onnx-and-tensorrt.md measured that the default arena
# rounds every allocation up the power-of-two curve, so a second session pays for
# that rounding twice - three 640x480 sessions hold 2642 MB with the defaults and
# 980 MB with this strategy. The template now requests it, and the label repeats
# the provider's own serialisation of the accepted keys, not the request.
#
# No gpu_mem_limit is set, on purpose: section 5 also measured that a limit is a cap
# the allocator fails on ("Available memory of 222494976 is smaller than requested
# bytes of 530841600"), not a budget it stays inside, and any fixed number is wrong
# for the next frame size.
#
# Machine: Windows 11, MSVC 14.50, onnxruntime 1.32.0. Command, both runs:
#   set ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT=<package>   then   templates\onnx-inference-ofx\test\test.bat Release
#
# 1. against the CUDA package (provider and CUDA DLLs): the label comes from the
#    contract harness, which reads the plug-in's own label parameter

